<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>x09 Group Policy Templates</displayName>
  <description>Group Policy Templates for x09</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="FirewallRulesList_Name">Firewall Rules Management</string>
      <string id="FirewallRulesList_Explain">Configure firewall rules.

Rule input format:
Action=Allow|Deny|Reject;Direction=In|Out;Protocol=TCP|UDP;Port=port_number;Source=IP-address;Destination=IP-address

Examples:
Action=Allow;Direction=In;Protocol=TCP;Port=80;Source=10.0.0.0/24;Destination=192.168.1.1
Action=Deny;Direction=Out;Protocol=UDP;Port=53;Source=192.168.1.0/24;Destination=8.8.8.8

Parameters:
- Action: Allow, Deny, Reject
- Direction: In (incoming), Out (outgoing)
- Protocol: TCP, UDP
- Port: port number (1-65535)
- Source: source IP address (can include mask)
- Destination: destination IP address (can include mask)

Each rule is saved as a separate line in the list.
A total of up to 10 rules can be added.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="FirewallRulesList">
        <listBox refId="FirewallRulesList" />
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
